nd other uh countries  have had public information campaigns  for example urging people to use energy  at off-peak times uh not just to save on  gas and electricity bills but just to  eat to even out uh demand and our  government seems to have really shied  away from from doing that and from  preparing people's uh mindset  um maybe they don't want to bum people  out any more than we've already been uh  you know I keep waiting for good news  and for uh things to start to get better  but they really seem to be just getting  uh worse and worse but um you know the  way that we're going to make sure that  things really don't get worse is to be  prepared for every eventuality and the  government could do more to kind of pave  the way for that Jake why do you think  the government hasn't prepared that the  public you know why aren't we being told  to unplug our plugs switch off lights do  our washing it you know out of peak  hours but why aren't we being told this  why why isn't there a government  information film that's being put out  there  I know a variety of reasons for that uh  one of which is that the government's  been quite busy with  trying to survive uh I mean there was  that period when Boris was sort of in  place but knew he was going that seemed  to be characterized by staces at the  heart of government when all this was  brewing and then we had the leadership  election of course and then we had  um you know Liz truss and dealing with  her mini budgets and all that so the  government's been quite quite busy  managing itself let alone managing the  country  um but also I think that the government  has perhaps not wanted to alarm people  and not wanted to um to give advice  about rationing and things which can  really affect people's sense of security  and confidence before it was absolutely  necessary and I think that's that's fair  enough really  um it like I say you know it may be that  we get through this winter without any  of these measures needing to be 